 "change": "One adapter after adapt_host_thread_class: adapt_remap_sweep_range (TextureCache.cs, Texture.cs, TexturePool.cs). At every guest Map or Unmap, TextureCache.MemoryUnmappedHandler queued an update of the pool mappings of every texture of its partially mapped set; each was then restored by TexturePool.ProcessDereferenceQueue and re-recorded and re-sent by every pool array that binds it. Now a member is swept only when the event can concern it: physically overlapped, never swept yet, without a pool owner, or with a pool owner of the event's address space whose range the event intersects. Host side (bridge, a contract input): MeloNXDiagnosticsReader decodes the engine's diagnostics report only when its bytes changed.",
 "preparation": "differs from the Core 733 preparation by the three files of the adapter",
 "device725": {
  "source": "IPA 725, Hogwarts Legacy, pid 51986, Core 731 (private journals, not in Git): the engine's 5.1 s performance samples",
  "arrayDeltas": "UpdateFromPoolDelta 390 to 570 calls per sample (4 to 5 a frame), 53 to 160 ids visited per call of which 88 % changed, 0.43 to 0.68 s of the GPU thread per sample, 18 to 34 KiB allocated per call, in the 20 s at 30 FPS as well",
  "compute": "compute dispatches 130 to 150 us each including the array deltas nested in them; 42 to 66 us without them; queue back-pressure 0 to 77 ms per sample; read copies 0.1 per dispatch",
  "gpuThread": "GPU thread dispatch 3.0 to 3.8 s of 5.1 s in the stretches at 20 to 22 FPS: 27 to 34 ms a frame"
 },
 "hostProfile": {
  "where": "scratchpad delta-profile/ (not in Git): copies of the Core 733 preparation, real TextureManager, TextureBindingsManager, TextureBindingsArrayCache, TexturePool, TextureCache, Texture and GPU MemoryManager over a fake backend; Linux x64, tiered compilation off; host figures are not device figures",
  "perId": "descriptor flip to an existing texture or remap keeping the mapping: 0.3 to 3 us per changed id; restore of a partially mapped texture 8 to 10 us and 352 B; a remap moving the mapping 23 to 108 us; a new texture 11 to 90 us",
  "sticky": "75 partially mapped textures, 4 array entries, an unrelated guest Map at every update: 664 to 850 us for the first entry and 26 to 31 KiB per call, 32 to 91 us for each following one; with the change the pool is not modified and no entry is updated (21 to 176 us per commit against 768 to 1 122)",
  "computeDispatch": "5.4 us per dispatch warm and 0 bytes on the host: the code path of a dispatch is not the device's cost"
 },
